  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1206 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nSadly, the triple digit temperatures and dry conditions are not done \nwith us yet. The stubborn upper ridging will remain over the region \nthrough at least the end of the work week. This regime will keep \nhighs near Heat Advisory temperatures with the hottest days looking \nto be Thursday and Friday. Highs on Wednesday and Friday will be \nclose to tying the record high at both KLBB and KCDS. Wednesday \nforecasted highs are 101 degrees at KLBB and 104 degrees at KCDS \nwith record highs of 102 degrees set in 19848 and 104 degrees set in \n1934, respectively. As for Friday, the forecast highs are 104 \ndegrees at KLBB and 106 degrees at KCDS with record highs of 106 \nmost recently set in 1957 and 2012 most recently set in 2012, \nrespectively. Subsidence from the upper ridging and little moisture \nwill keep conditions dry. An upper pattern change next weekend will \ncool temperatures, albeit only slightly, as well as possible \nprecipitation chances. Models indicate an upper trough will dig \nsouth across eastern CONUS later in the week, effectively pushing \nthe upper ridging west towards the Desert Southwest. The eastern \nedge of the ridging will remain over the region keeping \ntemperatures in the upper 90s to lower 100s. However, some embedded \nshortwaves will break the dry spell.",
